 5   │ 5   │  Garden                                                                  
 6   │ 6   │ ===========                                                              
 7   │ 7   │                                                                          
 8   │ 8   │                                                                          
 9   │ 9   │                                                                          
 10  │ 10  │ GENERAL                                                                  
 11  │ 11  │                                                                          
 12  │ 12  │ Dark Garden is a decorative outline font of unusual shape. The typeface  
 13  │ 13  │ is based on author's original hand drawings. The letterform is complex,  
 14  │ 14  │ with all characters decorated with spikes resembling thorns or flames,   
 15  │ 15  │ character spacing is very dense. Such a theme makes it a great font for  
 16  │ 16  │ titles, banners, logos etc.                                              
 17  │ 17  │                                                                          
 18  │ 18  │ As of version 1.1, Dark Garden includes letters of the English alphabet, 
 19  │ 19  │ Polish and German diacritic characters and some punctuation. Unicode     
 20  │ 20  │ encoding is used. The font is equipped with hinting information to allow 
 21  │ 21  │ high quality rendering at small point sizes. Only horizontal and         
 22  │ 22  │ vertical hints are currently used, future versions might take advantage  
 23  │ 23  │ of truetype hinting instructions some day. There are also a lot of       
 24  │ 24  │ kerning pairs defined in the font - they were chosen after looking at a  
 25  │ 25  │ choice of Polish and English texts and selecting the character pairs     
 26  │ 26  │ that needed manual kerning.                                              
 27  │ 27  │                                                                          
 28  │ 28  │ The font was created with PfaEdit / FontForge                            
 29  │ 29  │ (http://fontforge.sourceforge.net/) - an opensource font editing tool.   
 30  │ 30  │ Pfaedit uses its own text-based file format which can then be exported   
 31  │ 31  │ to truetype, postscript, opentype and many other font formats. This      
 32  │ 32  │ makes it possible to generate font files for Dark Garden in any of the   
 33  │ 33  │ many supported formats, so it can be used on almost any platform. So     
 34  │ 34  │ far, the truetype version has been tested on X11 (Linux) and Windows,    
 35  │ 35  │ the opentype version worked on Windows but not X11. Truetype should also 
 36  │ 36  │ work on Mac OS.                                                          
 37  │ 37  │                                                                          
 38  │ 38  │                                                                          
 39  │ 39  │                                                                          
 40  │ 40  │ INSTALLATION                                                             
 41  │ 41  │                                                                          
 42  │ 42  │ Installation is described for the truetype version of the font (which is 
 43  │ 43  │ what most users will need).                                              
 44  │ 44  │                                                                          
 45  │ 45  │ On Windows:                                                              
 46  │ 46  │ * Extract .ttf files from the archive into a temporary directory         
 47  │ 47  │ * In the Control Panel choose Fonts                                      
 48  │ 48  │ * From the File menu choose Install New Font                             
 49  │ 49  │ * Browse to the temporary directory you chose                            
 50  │ 50  │ * "Dark Garden" should appear in the font list - click OK (this may      
 51  │ 51  │   require Administrator privileges)                                      
 52  │ 52  │                                                                          
 53  │ 53  │ On Linux / UNIX (using KDE):                                             
 54  │ 54  │ * Extract .ttf files from the archive into a temporary directory         
 55  │ 55  │ * In the Control Center choose Font Installer in the System              
 56  │ 56  │   Administration tree                                                    
 57  │ 57  │ * Click on "Administrator Mode" and enter root's password                
 58  │ 58  │ * Click on "Add Fonts" icon                                              
 59  │ 59  │ * Select the .ttf file extracted from the archive and click OK           
 60  │ 60  │                                                                          
 61  │ 61  │ On Linux / UNIX (using commandline)                                      
 62  │ 62  │   unzip darkgarden-*.ttf.zip                                             
 63  │ 63  │   su                                                                     
 64  │ 64  │   ginstall -o root -m 644 DarkGardenMK.ttf /usr/X11R6/lib/fonts/TTF      
 65  │ 65  │   fc-cache -f                                                            
 66  │ 66  │                                                                          
 67  │ 67  │                                                                          
