 28  │ 28  │     """                                                                          
 29  │ 29  │     This class simply looks for occurrences of zero bytes, and infers            
 30  │ 30  │     whether the file is UTF16 or UTF32 (low-endian or big-endian)                
 31  │ 31  │     For instance, files looking like ( ␀ ␀ ␀ [nonzero] )+                     
 32  │ 32  │     have a good probability to be UTF32BE.  Files looking like ( ␀ [nonzero] )+ 
 33  │ 33  │     may be guessed to be UTF16BE, and inversely for little-endian varieties.     
