 26  │ 26  │ Subsampling                                                                                  
 27  │ 27  │ -----------                                                                                  
 28  │ 28  │                                                                                              
 29  │ 29  │ Subsampling is the practice of encoding images by implementing less resolution               
 30  │ 30  │ for chroma information than for luma information.                                            
 31  │ 31  │ (ref.: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chroma_subsampling)                                     
 32  │ 32  │                                                                                              
 33  │ 33  │ Possible subsampling values are 0, 1 and 2 that correspond to 4:4:4, 4:2:2 and               
 34  │ 34  │ 4:2:0.                                                                                       
 35  │ 35  │                                                                                              
 36  │ 36  │ You can get the subsampling of a JPEG with the                                               
 37  │ 37  │ :func:`.JpegImagePlugin.get_sampling` function.                                              
 38  │ 38  │                                                                                              
 39  │ 39  │ In JPEG compressed data a JPEG marker is used instead of an EXIF tag.                        
 40  │ 40  │ (ref.: https://exiv2.org/tags.html)                                                          
 41  │ 41  │                                                                                              
 42  │ 42  │                                                                                              
 43  │ 43  │ Quantization tables                                                                          
 44  │ 44  │ -------------------                                                                          
 45  │ 45  │                                                                                              
 46  │ 46  │ They are values use by the DCT (Discrete cosine transform) to remove                         
 47  │ 47  │ *unnecessary* information from the image (the lossy part of the compression).                
 48  │ 48  │ (ref.: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quantization_matrix#Quantization_matrices,              
 49  │ 49  │ https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JPEG#Quantization)                                             
 50  │ 50  │                                                                                              
 51  │ 51  │ You can get the quantization tables of a JPEG with::                                         
 52  │ 52  │                                                                                              
 53  │ 53  │   im.quantization                                                                            
 54  │ 54  │                                                                                              
 55  │ 55  │ This will return a dict with a number of lists. You can pass this dict                       
 56  │ 56  │ directly as the qtables argument when saving a JPEG.                                         
 57  │ 57  │                                                                                              
 58  │ 58  │ The quantization table format in presets is a list with sublists. These formats              
 59  │ 59  │ are interchangeable.                                                                         
 60  │ 60  │                                                                                              
 61  │ 61  │ Libjpeg ref.:                                                                                
 62  │ 62  │ https://web.archive.org/web/20120328125543/http://www.jpegcameras.com/libjpeg/libjpeg-3.html 
 63  │ 63  │                                                                                              
